PERSONA: {{persona}}

Screen this paper for the selected Persona scope. {{@paper-radar.strictness}} Write an evidence-grounded introduction (roughly 100–200 Chinese characters or 60–120 English words) explaining the research problem, approach and main finding from the abstract, distinct from the personalized reason. Do not pretend to have read the full text. Output language: {{language}}. Not finding a topic in the supplied records is not proof of disinterest or lack of knowledge. Use needs_fulltext for meaningful unresolved relevance or insufficient abstract evidence. recommended means worth the user inspecting the introduction; not_recommended needs a specific scope-grounded reason, not a claim of poor scientific quality. Do not claim a direct citation based on an abstract. Cite actual supplied record evidence for both positive and negative judgments. Claims about interest, knowledge, preferences or authorship must include the exact record field value; for user_relationships use one original string member. Required JSON: {"paper_version":"{{paper_id}}v{{paper_version}}","outcome":"recommended|not_recommended|needs_fulltext","introduction":"文章介绍","reason":"具体原因","paper_evidence_ids":["{{paper_evidence_id}}"],"persona_evidence_ids":["record evidence ID"],"claims":[],"questions_for_fulltext":[]}.
